WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:16.546
Thud, thud, thud.

2
00:00:16.547 --> 00:00:21.014
Joy smiled, opened her eyes, and sat up in bed.

3
00:00:21.015 --> 00:00:26.187
"Today is Saturday, and the walnuts are falling!" she cried.

4
00:00:26.188 --> 00:00:30.608
"What time is it?" asked Katie.

5
00:00:30.609 --> 00:00:34.090
"Time to rise and shine," said Joy.

6
00:00:34.091 --> 00:00:37.700
She jumped out of bed and ran to her desk.

7
00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:40.294
"Last night I did some figuring."

8
00:00:40.295 --> 00:00:42.974
She opened a small notebook.

9
00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:46.085
"I need one hundred dollars, right?

10
00:00:46.086 --> 00:00:52.016
And the nut-buying station will pay fifteen cents for each pound of walnuts.

11
00:00:52.017 --> 00:00:56.576
So I need to collect almost seven hundred pounds!"

12
00:00:56.577 --> 00:00:59.217
Katie gave her sister a funny look.

13
00:00:59.218 --> 00:01:02.122
"How did you figure that out?"

14
00:01:02.123 --> 00:01:06.653
"Dad helped me," said Joy. "But listen, I'm not done.

15
00:01:06.654 --> 00:01:10.941
Mom says I have to do my homework on school nights.

16
00:01:10.942 --> 00:01:16.272
So I have two weekends before the nut-buying station closes.

17
00:01:16.273 --> 00:01:21.584
Two weekends—only four days to meet my goal!"

18
00:01:21.585 --> 00:01:25.078
"Wow!" said Katie, jumping out of bed.

19
00:01:25.079 --> 00:01:27.440
"We'd better get busy!"

20
00:01:27.441 --> 00:01:29.888
"We?" said Joy.

21
00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:33.110
"Sure! I'll help," said Katie.

22
00:01:33.111 --> 00:01:36.462
"That's what a twin sister is for!"

23
00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:43.679
"Really? That's great, Katie! Thanks." Joy smiled.

24
00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:51.159
After breakfast Katie and Joy stepped out into the front yard wearing old jeans and sweatshirts.

25
00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:56.713
"A perfect day for walnuts!" said Joy. "Look at them!"

26
00:01:56.714 --> 00:02:02.486
The ground under the trees was covered with walnuts in their green hulls.

27
00:02:02.487 --> 00:02:07.288
Grandpa and Magoo came down the driveway with the garden cart.

28
00:02:07.289 --> 00:02:11.799
Grandpa lifted two big buckets out of the cart.

29
00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:14.246
"Here you go," he said.

30
00:02:14.247 --> 00:02:16.629
"I'll see you two at lunch!"

31
00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:20.449
The girls pulled on their work gloves.

32
00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:24.594
Joy picked up a walnut and threw it in her bucket.

33
00:02:24.595 --> 00:02:27.534
"That's one!" Joy said.

34
00:02:27.535 --> 00:02:32.098
Katie tossed a walnut in her bucket. "That's two!"

35
00:02:32.099 --> 00:02:37.511
The twins emptied buckets of walnuts into the cart all morning.

36
00:02:37.512 --> 00:02:41.048
By lunchtime the cart was half full.

37
00:02:41.049 --> 00:02:45.821
By three o'clock the ground under the first tree was clear.

38
00:02:45.822 --> 00:02:49.471
Joy poured her last bucket into the cart.

39
00:02:49.472 --> 00:02:52.350
"It's full!" she shouted.

40
00:02:52.351 --> 00:02:54.544
Then she ran toward the house.

41
00:02:54.545 --> 00:02:58.007
"Dad! The cart is full!"

42
00:02:58.008 --> 00:03:03.146
Joy and Katie watched eagerly as Dad hitched the cart to the car.

43
00:03:03.147 --> 00:03:08.554
Then Katie got in the backseat, and Joy jumped in the front with Dad.

44
00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:14.697
They drove out onto Blackberry Road, with the cart bouncing along behind.

45
00:03:14.698 --> 00:03:20.512
When they got to the recycling center, Dad backed the cart up to the hulling machine.

46
00:03:20.513 --> 00:03:23.347
The twins hopped out of the car.

47
00:03:23.348 --> 00:03:27.569
"Who collected all these nuts?" asked Mr. Ramirez.

48
00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:33.272
"Joy and I did," said Katie. "But they're Joy's nuts."

49
00:03:33.273 --> 00:03:38.871
"I'm going to use the money I earn to fix my great-grandma's fiddle," said Joy.

50
00:03:38.872 --> 00:03:45.407
Dad started shoveling walnuts into the bin, and Mr. Ramirez turned on the huller.

51
00:03:45.408 --> 00:03:49.277
"It's so noisy!" cried Katie.

52
00:03:49.278 --> 00:03:54.633
The girls covered their ears and watched the nuts being lifted into the huller.

53
00:03:54.634 --> 00:04:00.932
Then they ran around the machine and saw the walnuts shoot out into a big bag.

54
00:04:00.933 --> 00:04:03.752
The green hulls were gone.

55
00:04:03.753 --> 00:04:09.507
When the first bag got full, Mr. Ramirez put another bag in its place.

56
00:04:09.508 --> 00:04:13.979
The second bag filled up and then a third.

57
00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:19.466
When the fourth bag was almost half full, the hulling went silent.

58
00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:21.749
"That's all?" said Joy.

59
00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:25.142
"The whole cart fits into four bags?"

60
00:04:25.143 --> 00:04:30.084
"Let's weigh them and see how you did," said Mr. Ramirez.

61
00:04:30.085 --> 00:04:33.233
He peered at the numbers on the scale.

62
00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:35.652
"That's 170 pounds.

63
00:04:35.653 --> 00:04:42.362
So fifteen cents for each pound—that's twenty-five dollars and fifty cents."

64
00:04:42.363 --> 00:04:45.638
"YIPPEE!" cheered Joy.

65
00:04:45.639 --> 00:04:49.814
"I'm glad you brought your walnuts in early," said Mr. Ramirez.

66
00:04:49.815 --> 00:04:53.523
"On Monday morning the price drops to thirteen cents."

67
00:04:53.524 --> 00:05:00.313
"What? Oh no!" cried Joy.
